-- title:
--   Residual irreducibility at p when χ₀(Tₚ) is a non-unit
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero level with $p \nmid M$, and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers with $p \in S$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, and suppose $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $\chi_0$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal{O}'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (S \ {p})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S \setminus \{p\}$ together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$ with $q \notin S \setminus \{p\}$; in particular $T_p$ is among the generators, and it is assumed that $\chi_0(T_p)$ is not a unit of $\mathcal{O}'$. Assume also $p \neq 2$. Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $\mathcal{O}'$, i.e. a free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ together with a multiplicative map $\rho.\rho$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(V)$ which is continuous for the adic filtration (for each $n$ some finite subextension of $\mathbb{Q}$ has its pointwise stabiliser acting trivially on $V$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}^n V$). Assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \notin S \setminus \{p\}$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \chi_0(T_\ell) X + \ell$. The conclusion is that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit, the only subspaces $L$ of the residual representation space $\mathcal{O}'/\mathfrak{m} \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} V$ (with the base-changed action) that are stable under all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ are $L = \bot$ and $L = \top$.
--
--   This is the supersingular half of the local dichotomy at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level: when the $T_p$-eigenvalue of a weight-two point has positive valuation, the residual representation stays irreducible even after restriction to a decomposition group above $p$. It is used in the analysis of the local behaviour at $p$, being cited by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.unitRoot_sq_ne_one_of_point`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.unitRoot_sq_ne_one_of_point), [`CuspForm.point_dichotomy_at_exactly_dvd_of_ne_two`](thm.html#CuspForm.point_dichotomy_at_exactly_dvd_of_ne_two) and [`CuspForm.point_residual_trace_coinvariants_eq_residue_T`](thm.html#CuspForm.point_residual_trace_coinvariants_eq_residue_T).
